Nit: with `overflow: hidden` and no ellipsis, labels longer than the cap stop mid-word with no sign that they're cut. Going by the committed data, that's a few library names like `github.com/emicklei/go-restful/v3`, and about 15 second lines when sides are shown, like `client · otel-instrumentation-net_http` or `postgresql · otel-javaagent`. On the second line the part that gets cut is the distribution, which is what tells neighbouring columns apart.

Clipping each line instead would let it show an ellipsis, something like:

```css
.heatmap thead th.col b,
.heatmap thead th.col .secondary {
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
}
```

